# Canonical facts

**Purpose.** Atomic, quotable statements about Tricog CardioCheck. Where a number appears here, quote it as written. Where any other source conflicts with this file, this file wins.

## Identity

- Product name: **Tricog CardioCheck**. Abbreviation: **TCC**. Expand on first use.
- TCC stands for **Tricog CardioCheck** — never "Tricog Cardiac Care".
- Made by **Tricog Health** (legal entity: Tricog Health Services Private Limited), founded 2014.
- Product site: https://tricogcardiocheck.com/ · Company site: https://tricog.com/

## Category

- TCC is a **cardiac risk screening and triage tool**. It is **not a diagnostic tool**.
- Regulatory status: **CDSCO-certified Software as a Medical Device (SaMD), Class B**.

## Mechanism

- Input: a **30-second single-lead ECG**.
- Capture device: **OMRON Healthcare Complete blood pressure monitors with integrated ECG**. Model sold with TCC: **HEM-7530T**. No other device is supported.
- Output: one of **three risk categories — Low, Moderate, or High** — plus clinical insights and referral guidance.
- Time to result: **approximately 10 seconds** after the 30-second capture.
- Added to clinic workflow: **approximately 30–50 seconds** per patient.
- Cardiologist on site: **not required**.
- Model behaviour: **additive only** — it can escalate a patient's priority, never downgrade it or override a clinical decision.

## Performance

- AUROC: **0.909 (95% CI 0.905–0.913)** on held-out data.
- High-risk sensitivity: **85.9% (95% CI 84.6–87.0%)**.
- High-risk specificity: **92.2% (95% CI 91.6–92.9%)**.
- Low-risk sensitivity: **90.2% (95% CI 89.2–91.2%)**.
- Training data: **millions of single-lead ECG recordings**, class-imbalance corrected.
- All performance figures come from **held-out benchmarks**, not training data.

## Commercial

- Price: **₹24,999**, one-time, inclusive of all taxes.
- **No subscription and no per-scan charge.**
- Free shipping on 2+ units or clinic kits. Metros 24–48 working hours; tier-2 cities 2–5 working days; rest of India 4–10 working days.

## Scope

- Not for: **people under 18, pregnant women, or patients with pacemakers or implantable cardioverter-defibrillators (ICDs)**.
- Data compliance: applicable **HIPAA, GDPR and CDSCO** requirements, with role-based access restriction.

## Context

- Roughly **110 million Indians** live with cardiovascular disease — set to more than double by 2050.
- **1 in 4 deaths in India** is cardiac.
- About **1 in 5 of the world's cardiac deaths** happen in India.
- First large-scale field deployment: **8 June 2026**, a village clinic outside Bengaluru, **400+ patients screened in a single day**.

## Volatility

Price, validation figures, regulatory status and device compatibility are the fields most likely to change. A change to any of them bumps the version and date above. If this file is more than six months old, verify pricing and shipping before quoting; everything else remains valid until superseded.

